"essay": "Nowadays, an increasing number of women tend to give birth later in their life. This could be attributed to multiple factors, which will be analyzed in the essay below, together with the reasons why this trend became common.\n\nThere are two reasons why women are having children later. The first one is the greater emphasis  they place on their professional and academic advancements on the grounds that they are significantly influenced by modern thoughts and lifestyles. This could be exemplified in China where the child-rearing expenditure is increasing dramatically, which ultimately lead the childbirth rate to a significant decrease. Another reason is that women nowadays hold senior positions in organizations. More specifically,  if they have an important role in organizations, they will have various priorities to spend time on, which is synonymous with they no longer have availability for maternal duty.\n\nFrom my point of view, the benefits and drawbacks of this issue impact equally on both individuals and society. To begin with, delaying childbirth gives women room to accumulate life experience and wealth possession, allowing them to become financially strong. This is very likely to make their children enjoy their family when they grow up as a result. However, not only the mother but also the children face the elevated risk of health issues if the children are born late. For example, as the mothers grow old, there is a high probability that pregnancy or delivery complications such as deformity, infertility and in the worst-case scenario, death, will occur.\n\nIn summary, the fact that women are reluctant to welcome new members in their family is caused by multiple factors. From my perspective, emphasizing on advancements and being able to hold senior positions are two primary reasons." 
